config BR2_PACKAGE_REVPI_PICONTROL
	bool "revpi-picontrol"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	help
	  KUNBUS piControl, the Revolution Pi PiBridge master and
	  process-image driver. It creates /dev/piControl0, through which
	  the edge agent's revpi-io backend reads and writes the process
	  image of the Revolution Pi Connect 4 and the modules on its
	  PiBridge (ADR-048 DEC-8.8).

	  piControl is an out-of-tree module and is not part of the KUNBUS
	  kernel tree: it is built against the pinned KUNBUS kernel of the
	  same image as a signed module (the build's module signing key
	  signs it in modules_install, so a kernel that enforces module
	  signatures loads it) and is loaded at boot by
	  systemd-modules-load.

	  The package version is the piControl release that KUNBUS builds
	  for the pinned kernel; it must be bumped together with the kernel
	  (docs/hardware/revpi-connect4.md).

	  https://gitlab.com/revolutionpi/piControl

comment "revpi-picontrol needs a Linux kernel and an aarch64 target"
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL || !BR2_aarch64
